# Modules
#
# `modules/*`, not `modules/`: git cannot re-include anything inside an excluded
# *directory*, so the negations below were decorative — `modules/tasks/` only
# stayed in version control because it had been added to the index before the
# rule existed. Matching the children instead makes the exceptions real.
#
# Bundled, first-party packages are tracked. Everything else under `modules/` is
# an installed payload and belongs to the operator, not to this repository.
#
# **Every first-party package must be listed below.** Missing one does not fail
# loudly: Tailwind skips gitignored files, so the package's UI silently loses any
# utility class that no other file in the project happens to use. That is how
# `pl-12` vanished from the money input and left the currency symbol sitting
# underneath the value.

# modules/*
# !modules/tasks/
# !modules/announcements/
# !modules/ecommerce/
# !modules/paths.ts
# !modules/registry.ts
# !modules/tsconfig.json
# !modules/types.ts